# PCA of forms of capital, 100-year time slices (4300-500 BCE, n=39 centuries)

**Main run:** all 12 capital forms, correlation PCA (each column re-standardised, ddof=1),
one global PCA on the century matrix (`capital.csv`, parsed with `decimal=","`).
Reported loadings = corr(variable, PC score). Sign convention: PC1 positive for the majority
of forms; PC2 sign fixed by neutral rule (max |loading| made positive = Axes&Celts).

## Variance
PC1 30.3 %, PC2 19.5 % (PC1+PC2 = 49.8 %; PC3 12.9 %, PC4 12.5 %). Invariant to ddof (0 vs 1: 0.00 pp).

