## Robustness
* Jackknife (leave one century out, 39 runs): HouseSize largest |PC2| of the trio 39/39; trio PC1 all
  positive 39/39; trio PC2 same sign 39/39. LOO ranges: HouseSize PC1 0.34-0.50, PC2 0.45-0.58;
  Dagger PC1 0.44-0.57, PC2 0.03-0.21; HatchetSword PC1 0.49-0.66, PC2 0.03-0.14. Variance PC1 28.6-31.8 %, PC2 17.8-20.4 %.
* 37 centuries (drop 4300/4200 BCE, i.e. only those present in time_series_data.csv): PC1 signs identical
  12/12, corr of PC1 loadings 0.996; trio PC1 +0.336/+0.457/+0.545 (ranks 10/9/7), trio PC2 +0.512/+0.283/+0.198
  (ranks 3/7/11). Variance PC1 32.4 %, PC2 16.4 %. **No qualitative change.**
* Covariance PCA on raw Z: trio PC1 +0.431/+0.529/+0.570 (ranks 10/6/5), PC2 +0.551/+0.181/+0.101 (ranks 5/8/12). Same picture.
* Eigenvector vs correlation-loading: identical rank orders for the trio, Spearman 1.000 on both PCs.
* Symbolic-trio-only PCA (diagnostic, NOT the answer): PC1 54.4 % (all three 0.63-0.85), PC2 28.8 % with
  HouseSize -0.57 vs HatchetSword +0.74 - a within-trio axis that does not carry over to the 12-variable space.
* Rolling 15-century windows (appendix, signs aligned to global solution): large local instability
  (trio PC1 sd 0.34-0.62, PC2 sd 0.37-0.67) - confirms loadings must be read from the global solution.

## Final hypothesis
In the PCA of the twelve forms of capital analysed in hundred-year slices, the symbolic-capital
components sit in the **middle band of PC1, all on the same (positive, "accumulation") side**, and are
**strongly unequally distributed along PC2**.
